=begin pod :kind("Type") :subkind("class") :category("basic")

=TITLE class RakuAST::Type::Capture

=SUBTITLE Represent a type without any additional features

    class RakuAST::Type::Capture { }

The C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> class represents a stand-in Raku type
with an optional type-smiley.

=head2 Object introspection

C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> object is typically created when parsing
Raku Programming Language code.  So most developers will only need to
know how to introspect the objects created.

=head3 definite

=begin code :preamble<my $type>
say $type.definite;  # True, False or Bool
=end code

Returns C<True> if a defined constraint was indicated ("D"), C<False>
if a B<not> defined constraint was indicated ("U"), or the C<Bool>
enum if no constraint was indicated ("_" or "" or no smiley).

=head3 name

=begin code :preamble<my $type>
say $type.name;  # RakuAST::Name.from-identifier("foo")
=end code

Returns the C<L<RakuAST::Name>|/type/RakuAST/Name> object of this
C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> object.

=head3 smiley

=begin code :preamble<my $type>
say $type.smiley;  # "D", "U" or ""
=end code

Returns whatever was (possibly implicitely) specified with the
C<.smiley> named argument at object creation.

=head2 Object creation

There are several ways to create a C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> object.
For simple identifiers it is recommended to use the alternate
C<.from-identifier> method to create a C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> object.
Otherwise one can use the standard C<.new> method.

=head3 new

=begin code
my $type = RakuAST::Type::Capture.new(
  RakuAST::Name.from-identifier("D"),
  :smiley<D>
);
dd $type;  # ::T:D
=end code

Creates a C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> object from the given
L<C<RakuAST::Name>|/type/RakuAST/Name> object and an optional
C<:smiley> named argument that should be one of "D", "U", "_" or "".

=head3 from-identifier

=begin code
my $type = RakuAST::Type::Capture.from-identifier('T', :smiley<D>);
dd $type;  # ::T:D
=end code

Creates a C<RakuAST::Type::Capture> object from the given simple
identifier string (which may B<not> contain any C<::> separators),
and an optional smiley string.

=end pod
